    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17075" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">explĭcātus</span></b> ,
			ūs, m.
		explico, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an unfolding</i>, <i>stretching
			apart.</i> * </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">alterno crurum explicatu,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					8, 42, 67, § 166</span></i>
			.— * </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, of speech, <i>an
				explication</i>, <i>exposition</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">(natura deorum) quam difficiles explicatus
					haberet,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					N. D. 3, 39, 93</span></i>
			.</div>
